==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|congénère}}, from {{uder|en|la|-}} {{compound|la|com-|genus|t1=same|t2=kind|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|en|/ˈkɒnd͡ʒɪnə/|/kənˈd͡ʒiːnə(ɹ)/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[plant]] or [[animal]] of the same [[taxonomic]] [[genus]] as another.
# A person or thing similar in behavior or nature to another.
#* '''1902''', {{w|William James}}, ''The Varieties of Religious Experience'', Lecture I:
#*: Not that we may thereby swamp the thing in the wholesale condemnation which we pass on its inferior '''congeners''', but rather that we may by contrast ascertain the more precisely in what its merits consist, by learning at the same time to what particular dangers of corruption it may also be exposed.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Any of a group of structurally-related compounds.
# Any of several [[alcohol]]s, other than [[ethanol]], that are found in [[fermented]] and [[distilled]] [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]s, and are partially responsible for their [[flavour]] and [[character]].

